## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

### Implementation Summary

#### 1. Fetched Latest Documentation
- Retrieved official installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Confirmed framework-specific setup instructions for Next.js App Router

#### 2. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json accordingly

#### 3. Configuration Changes
- **Modified:** `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx`
  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body tag (after Toaster component)
  - Follows Next.js App Router pattern as documented in official Vercel docs

### Files Modified
1. `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
2. `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and dependencies
3. `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

### Implementation Approach
- Preserved existing code structure and styling
- Added Analytics component at the optimal location (end of body tag)
- Followed official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router projects
- No breaking changes to existing functionality

### Verification Steps Completed
✓ Package installed successfully using npm
✓ Build completed successfully with no errors
✓ TypeScript compilation passed
✓ Linter run completed (no new errors introduced)
✓ All 16 pages generated successfully in production build

### Next Steps for User
To activate Web Analytics:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to your Vercel dashboard → Analytics section
3. Click the "Enable" button to activate analytics tracking
4. Once enabled, analytics will automatically start collecting page view data

### Notes
- The Analytics component is client-side and has zero impact on server-side rendering
- Analytics will only collect data when deployed on Vercel (not in local development)
- The implementation follows the exact pattern specified in the latest Vercel documentation
